{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Peter's Job Interview"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "No News Is Good News"}, {"type": "position", "content": 9}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 8}, {"type": "level", "content": "A1.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Exchange information on instructions about basic activities and safety at work.  "}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level.  "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Understands key information in written texts about the communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level.  "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Understands key information in written texts about the communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level.  "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Understands key information in written texts about the communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Understands key information in written texts about the communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level.  "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Giving and Responding to Bad News"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "There are different ways to give and respond to bad news."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Examples</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Giving bad news </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I've got some bad news for you! <br />I regret to inform you that ... <br />I'm sorry but ... <br />Unfortunately, </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Responding to bad news </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Oh no/dear! <br />I can't believe it! <br />I'm sorry to hear that ... <br />That's unfortunate/awful! <br />I know how you must be feeling!</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "news "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "new information "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I have some bad news!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le08ob09aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use when you give or respond to bad news."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to stress"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to feel very worried  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Waiting for a call is stressing me out."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le08ob09aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to take your mind off things"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to spend time away from something  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Let's go to the park. It helps to take your mind off things."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le08ob09aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to come up "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to appear "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: My e-mails aren't coming up."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le08ob09aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to regret "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to say that you are sorry for something. "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I regret to inform you that it is raining outside."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le08ob09aud05"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn2le08ob09re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Present Simple Tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Use the Present Simple to talk about facts and usual actions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "To form the negative, use do / does not  before the verb. </br>Do not add s to the verb when used with he, she, it.</br> Pay attention to the short form. It's used in talking.</br></br>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "To form a yes/no question, use do/does and change the word order like this:         \tDo / Does + subject + verb </br>Do not add s to the verb with he, she, it."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I really want this job!"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Don't worry."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Write a short dialogue about bad news (6-8 lines)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Your friend's phone is not working. They share the bad news with you."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Respond to their bad news."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use simple connectors like <span class=\"italic\">and</span>, <span class=\"italic\">or</span>, <span class=\"italic\">but</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Practice your dialogue with a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I share bad news with a friend."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I respond to bad news."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn2le08ob09re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn2le08ob09re2img05.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn2le08ob09re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Hey Peter! What are you doing? Did you get a call?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:      I'm checking my e-mail. Unfortunately, no news about the interview!<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I know how you must be feeling, but you know what they say, no news is good news!<br>", "id": 1, "time": "10", "image": "engenn2le08ob09re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:      I really want this job!<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Don't worry!<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:      I don't think they like me. I'm stressing out! Nothing is coming up!<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: It's sunny outside! Why don't we go out and do something? It can help take your mind off things.", "id": 2, "time": "16000", "image": "engenn2le08ob09re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>:      Great idea, but I regret to tell you that it's supposed to rain.<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Oh dear! That's unfortunate! You are funny, Peter! We could go to the park or we can go the museum!<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Let's go to the museum.", "id": 3, "time": "32500", "image": "engenn2le08ob09re2img03.jpg"}]}}]}], "exercises": [{"questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "id": 0, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "L